             In this special case, you can fetch the dataset from the original\n128 |             source::\n129 | \n130 |                 import pandas as pd\n131 |                 import numpy as np\n132 | \n133 |                 data_url = \"http://lib.stat.cmu.edu/datasets/boston\"\n134 |                 raw_df = pd.read_csv(data_url, sep=\"\\\\s+\", skiprows=22, header=None)\n135 |                 data = np.hstack([raw_df.values[::2, :], raw_df.values[1::2, :2]])\n136 |                 target = raw_df.values[1::2, 2]\n137 | \n138 |             Alternative datasets include the California housing dataset and the\n139 |             Ames housing dataset. You can load the datasets as follows::\n140 | \n141 |                 from sklearn.datasets import fetch_california_housing\n142 |                 housing = fetch_california_housing()\n143 | \n144 |             for the California housing dataset and::\n145 | \n146 |                 from sklearn.datasets import fetch_openml\n147 |                 housing = fetch_openml(name=\"house_prices\", as_frame=True)\n148 | \n149 |             for the Ames housing dataset.\n150 | \n151 |             [1] M Carlisle.\n152 |             \"Racist data destruction?\"\n153 |             <https://medium.com/@docintangible/racist-data-destruction-113e3eff54a8>\n154 | \n155 |             [2] Harrison Jr, David, and Daniel L. Rubinfeld.\n156 |             \"Hedonic housing prices and the demand for clean air.\"\n157 |             Journal of environmental economics and management 5.1 (1978): 81-102.\n158 |             <https://www.researchgate.net/publication/4974606_Hedonic_housing_prices_and_the_demand_for_clean_air>\n159 |             \"\"\"\n160 |         )\n161 |         raise ImportError(msg)\n162 |     try:\n163 |         return globals()[name]\n164 |     except KeyError:\n165 |         # This is turned into the appropriate ImportError\n166 |         raise AttributeError\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"_to_new_tags\"...\n### Sea