dex_name = self._get_index_name()\n1337 | \n1338 |         if condition:\n1339 |             # irregular TS rotated 30 deg. by default\n1340 |             # probably a better place to check / set this.\n1341 |             if not self._rot_set:\n1342 |                 self.rot = 30\n1343 |             format_date_labels(ax, rot=self.rot)\n1344 | \n1345 |         if index_name is not None and self.use_index:\n1346 |             ax.set_xlabel(index_name)\n```\n"}, {"content": "Based on the search results, the following functions and classes seem relevant for implementing the requested feature of grouping columns in subplots:\n\n```\npandas/plotting/_matplotlib/core.py\nfunction: MPLPlot._setup_subplots\n\npandas/plotting/_matplotlib/core.py\nfunction: MPLPlot._adorn_subplots\n\npandas/plotting/_matplotlib/core.py\nfunction: MPLPlot._get_subplots\n\npandas/plotting/_matplotlib/core.py\nfunction: MPLPlot._get_axes_layout\n\npandas/plotting/_matplotlib/core.py\nfunction: LinePlot._post_plot_logic\n```\n\nLet's now examine the `_setup_subplots` function in detail to understand how it could be modified to support grouping columns.\n\n<function=get_entity_contents>\n<parameter=entity_names>['pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/core.py:MPLPlot._setup_subplots']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "get_entity_contents", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for entity `pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/core.py:MPLPlot._setup_subplots`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/core.py:MPLPlot._setup_subplots`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/core.py:MPLPlot._setup_subplots`.\n```\n372 | def _setup_subplots(self):\n373 |         if self.subplots:\n374 |             fig, axes = create_subplots(\n375 |                 naxes=self.nseries,\n376 |                 sharex=self.sharex,\n377 |                 sharey=self.sharey,\n378 |     